    "12.20"
  ],
  "description": "A-601's Tuesday revisions of Door 107 and Door 117 from \"1.5 h\" to \"90 min\" are recorded as change stories and approved on Tuesday evening; chg-17, in wing P, is governed by the fixture policy. On Wednesday the project and wing P are normalized under the fixture fire-rating interpretation, which leaves both revisions changing nothing; the approved stories are untouched. On Thursday each approval is withdrawn. The story does not reopen: the withdrawal's write records a period of no length, a begin act citing the withdrawal and an end act at the same instant citing the normalization, and under the fixture policy also that policy's end act with the same content. From Thursday the story reads ended and unreviewed, with the normalization as its ending; a Wednesday frame still shows the approval as its ending. No listing read counts it. A Friday normalization of the project to literal comparison makes chg-7's revision a change again, and its write records the related change story chg-7+1.",
  "note": "7.6.2: \"Where the interpretation in force at that withdrawal's effective time leaves the revision changing no property, the period that begins then also ends then, with the normalization that put that interpretation in force as its ending record. That period has no length, is never open (7.6.3) and is the story's last: the story's ending is the review up to that instant, and the normalization from it (7.6.14).\" 6.7.9: \"Withdrawing a review returns the story to `unreviewed` from the withdrawal's effective time ... Where no other review remains in effect and that interpretation leaves the revision changing no property, the story stays ended, and from then its ending is the normalization that put that interpretation in force (7.6.2).\" README section 5, Ending policies, *Normalization endings*: \"A change story's period that a normalization ends under the baseline (7.2.7, 7.6.2), including a period of no length that begins at a review's withdrawal, ends under the policy in the same way, with the same content.\" 7.3.8 *After it* applies to a story whose baseline ending is a normalization \"as a period ending\".",
